Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against jin-s13/xtcocoapi]

get_version() execs version.py and then reads its names back via locals().
Two separate bugs combine here. (1) It only takes the short_version branch
when 'sdist' or 'bdist_wheel' is literally in sys.argv, and otherwise reads
__version__ from the else branch; a modern pip calls
prepare_metadata_for_build_wheel with 'dist_info' in sys.argv, not
'bdist_wheel', hitting that else branch. (2) More fundamentally, the exec+
locals() pattern itself breaks under PEP 667 (Python 3.13+): locals() inside
a function is now always a fresh snapshot built from the function's static
fast-locals, so names that are only ever created by the exec'd code (never
assigned anywhere in get_version's own source, on either branch) are not
visible through a later locals() call at all, independent of sys.argv. That
is why cp313/cp314/cp314t fail at the metadata-prep step while cp312 (an
older Python without PEP 667) does not; it is not riscv64-specific and
reproduces with any 3.13+ interpreter on any arch, with any sufficiently new
pip. Fixing only (1), as this patch originally did, still failed here with
KeyError: 'short_version' instead of KeyError: '__version__' - same root
cause, different branch. Execing into an explicit namespace dict sidesteps
locals() entirely and fixes both.

diff --git a/setup.py b/setup.py
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/setup.py
+++ b/setup.py
@@ -4,14 +4,23 @@
 version_file = 'xtcocotools/version.py'
 
 def get_version():
+    # Exec into an explicit namespace dict rather than relying on locals():
+    # under PEP 667 (Python 3.13+), locals() inside a function is always a
+    # fresh snapshot, so names only ever created by this exec (never assigned
+    # in get_version's own source) don't survive a later locals() call, on
+    # either branch below. Reproduces on any 3.13+ interpreter, independent
+    # of architecture.
+    version_locals = {}
     with open(version_file, 'r') as f:
-        exec(compile(f.read(), version_file, 'exec'))
+        exec(compile(f.read(), version_file, 'exec'), version_locals)
     import sys
     # return short version for sdist
-    if 'sdist' in sys.argv or 'bdist_wheel' in sys.argv:
-        return locals()['short_version']
+    # pip's build backend also runs prepare_metadata_for_build_wheel with
+    # 'dist_info'/'egg_info' in sys.argv, not 'bdist_wheel'; treat the same.
+    if {'sdist', 'bdist_wheel', 'dist_info', 'egg_info'} & set(sys.argv):
+        return version_locals['short_version']
     else:
-        return locals()['__version__']
+        return version_locals['__version__']
 
